            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "The CI verification failure is due to reasons unrelated to this patch.\nThe issue is currently being addressed in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/80413"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Josh Lehan",
                        "email": "krellan@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Krellan"
                    },
                    "message": "Good catch. There's a lot of various failure flags a sensor can have, and it's hard to know which flags were intended for which situations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Josh Lehan",
                        "email": "krellan@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Krellan"
                    },
                    "message": "I gave +2 to https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/80413 so once that is submitted, rebase this on top of it, then the CI will compile it again and it should compile then."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I have noticed that even if dbus missing operates normally, the sensor fail reason currently categorizes it as a bad reading, which should be incorrect.\nI am considering submitting another patch to add a flag similar to bad reading to address this issue.\nDo you think this approach is appropriate?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I have rebased and the CI verification has passed.\nAre there any further suggestions for modifications to this patch?"
                }
            ],
